ived":"2018-12-19","manufacturer":"Kia Motors America","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:HOSES, LINES/PIPING, AND FITTINGS","summary":"Kia Motors America (Kia) is recalling certain 2011-2017 Optima, 2012-2017 Sorento and 2011-2018 Sportage vehicles that previously received an engine replacement under recall number 17V-224, warranty, or the Knock Sensor Detection System (KSDS) Product Improvement Campaign.  The high pressure fuel pipe that connects to the fuel pump outlet may have been damaged, misaligned or improperly torqued during the engine replacement procedure, possibly causing a fuel leak.","consequence":"A fuel leak in the presence of an ignition source can increase the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Kia has notified owners, and dealers will inspect and replace the fuel pipe, as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began January 17, 2019.  Owners may contact Kia customer service at 1-800-333-4542.  Kia's number for this recall is SC172.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":71653,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V907000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":21,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2013","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2012","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2013","make":"KIA","model":"SORENTO"},{"year":"2012","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2011","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2011","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2014","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2012","make":"KIA","model":"SORENTO"},{"year":"2013","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2014","make":"KIA","model":"SORENTO"},{"year":"2015","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2014","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2015","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2015","make":"KIA","model":"SORENTO"},{"year":"2016","make":"KIA","model":"SORENTO"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2016","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"SORENTO"},{"year":"2016","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"KIA","model":"SPORTAGE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V161000","received":"2018-03-08","manufacturer":"Kia Motors America","component":"HYBRID PROPULSION SYSTEM","summary":"Kia Motors America (Kia) is recalling certain 2017-2018 Kia Optima hybrid vehicles.  These vehicles are equipped with a Voltage Protection Device (VPD), designed to protect the high voltage battery module, that may activate inadvertently.","consequence":"If the VPD activates while the vehicle is being operated in Electric Vehicle (EV) mode, there may be a loss of power, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Kia will notify owners, and dealers will remove the VPD switch and install two newly designed Battery Management Systems (BMS) that contain Overvoltage Protection Devices (OPDs), free of charge.  The recall is expected to begin May 2018.  Owners may contact Kia customer service at 1-800-333-4542.  Kia's number for this recall is SC162.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1710,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V161000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V594000","received":"2023-08-24","manufacturer":"Kia America, Inc.","component":"LATCHES/LOCKS/LINKAGES:TRUNK LID:LATCH","summary":"Kia America, Inc. (Kia) is recalling certain 2016-2017 Rio, 2016-2018 Optima, 2017-2018 Optima Hybrid and Optima Plug-in Hybrid vehicles.  The trunk latch base may crack, preventing the opening of the trunk from the inside.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard number 401, \"Internal Trunk Release.\"","consequence":"A person inside the trunk compartment may become trapped, increasing their risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the trunk latch base subassembly, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed October 19, 2023.  Owners may contact Kia customer service at 1-800-333-4542.  Kia's number for this recall is SC278.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":319436,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V594000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":9,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2016","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2016","make":"KIA","model":"RIO"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA HYBRID"},{"year":"2018","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA HYBRID"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA PHEV"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"KIA","model":"OPTIMA PHEV"},{"year":"2017","make":"KIA","model":"RIO"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
